  "prepare:exodus-19-18:0": "{\"model\":\"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"You write a SECTION LOOK for an illustrated edition: one short shared visual description reused by every image of a story section, so that independently generated images of the section agree with each other. Return only JSON.\\nRules: each value is one or two short phrases, at most 200 characters. Describe only what stays the same across the whole section: place, time of day, weather, light, and situational clothing or props. Leave out poses, actions and individual moments, and do not restate anyone's fixed appearance; canon does that. If the section spans a change (night into morning), say so once. Obey the work brief's depiction rules. Mention no text or written elements.\\nCast marked hasForm: false have no body and are never drawn. Describe only the shared place, weather and light. Where the section shows one of them, its presence may appear only as smoke, cloud, fire, wind or light spread through the place. Never describe its throne, seat, chariot, robe, train, face, hands, hair, body or silhouette, even as an empty seat, a denial or a figure made of light: bodily words in the text are metaphors. Keep formed characters' own situational clothing and props attached to them. The cast list covers the whole section; do not force every cast member into the shared setting or add individual poses, actions or moments.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"WORK BRIEF\\nTone: Reverent, grounded and epic; grief, hope and human dignity without spectacle.\\nDepiction rules:\\n- God the Father has no human face or body; use light, cloud, fire or radiance. The Holy Spirit is dove, wind or flame, never human.\\n- Treat battles, death and crucifixion seriously; avoid lingering gore.\\n- No sexually explicit content; non-sexual nudity may follow the text.\\n- Show all peoples with dignity, without ethnic or religious caricature.\\n- Visionary creatures follow the 