pic\"],\"allow_fallbacks\":false},\"reasoning\":{\"effort\":\"none\"},\"max_tokens\":900,\"usage\":{\"include\":true}}",
  "prepare:exodus-19-18:1": "{\"model\":\"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"You plan one illustration of one moment of a work's text. You get the moment with its neighbours in the same story section, the work brief, the era, the section cast and a SECTION LOOK GUIDE. Return only JSON.\\n- Draw one scene at one instant: no collage and no sequence of steps. If the moment recounts several actions, pick one representative instant. If it has no event (a list, genealogy, law, saying or greeting), illustrate its content or setting through people, places and things, never as a written document.\\n- Show what the moment is about. When the moment is mostly someone's words (a prophecy, oracle, poem, proverb, prayer, letter, argument or teaching, or a story, parable, vision or memory being told), draw what the words describe and leave the speaker, writer and listeners out, unless the text shows them inside that scene (a visionary within the vision). Never put a speaker, writer or listener into a scene their words only describe, and never make them a figure of their own words, such as the king ready for battle or the man standing in the gap.\\n- In `selectedCast`, list every section cast entry that will be visible: people, groups, places, objects, and any presence without form shown through its effects. Give a few words of the text for each. Leave out cast who are elsewhere or only mentioned. Anyone without a cast entry may appear as an unnamed role or crowd when the moment needs them.\\n- Describe pose, action, placement and situational detail. Leave fixed appearance to canon, name no art style, and ask for no visible writing: scrolls, tablets, letters and books stay rolled or closed, and signs and boards are blank. Describe only what can be seen; leave out unseen or invisible beings, because anything named gets drawn. Keep every depiction rule.\\n- The scene fields carry this moment's place, time, light and situational clothing. The SECTION LOOK GUIDE is a suggestion for them: keep what fits this moment and change what does not. OWNER LOOK CONSTRAINTS, when given instead, are binding: keep the setting and time of day consistent with them.\\n- Each field is one or two short phrases.\\n- Cast marked hasForm: false have no body and are never drawn. When the moment shows one of them appearing or acting, select it and show the moment through the place and the people who witness it. In the scene fields, describe in your own plain words only the physical effects the text names, such as smoke, cloud, fire, storm, wind or light filling a place, spread through the scene or coming from beyond the frame rather than gathered into one glowing shape. Never name it or call it seated, standing, enthroned or riding, and leave out its throne, seat, chariot, robe, train or hem and any face, hands, hair or body: bodily words in the text are metaphors. Say only where those effects are. Whenever the scene keeps light, cloud or fire that comes from it, select it. Keep the people and the place as the subject of the image. A command, oath or mention alone is not an appearance, so add no effect for it then.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"WORK BRIEF\\nTone: Reverent, grounded and epic; grief, hope and human dignity without spectacle.\\nDepiction rules:\\n- God the Father has no human face or body; use light, cloud, fire or radiance. The Holy Spirit is dove, wind or flame, never human.\\n- Treat battles, death and crucifixion seriously; avoid lingering gore.\\n- No sexually explicit content; non-sexual nudity may follow the text.\\n- Show all peoples with dignity, without ethnic or religious caricature.\\n- Visionary creatures follow the text, strange and fearsome rather than comic.\\nEra: Egypt, wilderness and settlement. People: Israelites, Egyptians and neighboring ancient peoples. Dress: Woven tunics, cloaks, Egyptian linen and priestly garments. Technology: Bronze tools, chariots and early iron; no modern objects.\\nSTORY SECTION: The LORD descends on Sinai\\n\\nMOMENT (Exodus 19:18): Mount Sinai, the whole of it, smoked, because Yahweh descended on it in fire; and its smoke ascended like the smoke of a furnace, and the whole mountain quaked greatly.\\nPREVIOUS: Moses led the people out of the camp to meet God; and they stood at the lower part of the mountain.\\nNEXT: When the sound of the trumpet grew louder and louder, Moses spoke, and God answered him by a voice.\\n\\nCAST ON STAGE IN THIS SECTION (id: name):\\n- moses: Moses (hasForm: true)\\n- god: God / Yahweh, the Father and God of Israel (hasForm: false)\\n- mount_sinai: Mount Sinai (hasForm: true)\\n\\nSECTION LOOK GUIDE (a suggestion; keep what fits this moment):\\n{\\\"place\\\":\\\"The gravel plain below a smoking mountain\\\",\\\"timeOfDay\\\":\\\"Morning\\\",\\\"weather\\\":\\\"Thick cloud and smoke over the summit\\\",\\\"light\\\":\\\"Fire glowing through smoke\\\",\\\"clothing\\\":\\\"Wool cloaks and head coverings\\\"}\"}],\"response_format\":{\"type\":\"json_schema\",\"json_schema\":{\"name\":\"scene_plan\",\"strict\":true,\"schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"focusQuote\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"A few words copied from MOMENT naming what this image shows.\"},\"instant\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"One sentence fixing the single instant to draw: who is where, doing what.\"},\"selectedCast\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"entryId\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"moses\",\"god\",\"mount_sinai\"]},\"evidence\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"A few words from the text that put this entry in the scene.\"}},\"required\":[\"entryId\",\"evidence\"],\"additionalProperties\":false},\"description\":\"Every section cast entry visible in the image, once each: people, groups, places, objects and presences shown through effects. Empty when none is.\"},\"primarySubject\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The main subject and its pose or placement at that instant. For a cast entry with hasForm false, describe only the smoke, cloud, fire, wind or light the text names, never the entry itself. One or two short phrases.\"},\"action\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"What happens at that one instant. For a cast entry with hasForm false, describe only the smoke, cloud, fire, wind or light the text names, never the entry itself. One or two short phrases.\"},\"setting\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The physical place and surroundings, consistent with the text and era. One or two short phrases.\"},\"secondaryElements\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Supporting people, props and effects with their placement. One or two short phrases.\"},\"mood\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The emotional atmosphere of the moment. One or two short phrases.\"},\"timeOfDay\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"This moment's time of day, weather and situational light. One or two short phrases.\"},\"composition\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Viewpoint, framing and placement of the subjects, independent of art style. One or two short phrases.\"}},\"required\":[\"focusQuote\",\"instant\",\"selectedCast\",\"primarySubject\",\"action\",\"setting\",\"secondaryElements\",\"mood\",\"timeOfDay\",\"composition\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},\"provider\":{\"require_parameters\":true,\"order\":[\"anthropic\"],\"allow_fallbacks\":false},\"reasoning\":{\"effort\":\"none\"},\"max_tokens\":2400,\"usage\":{\"include\":true}}",
  "prepare:exodus-19-18:2": "{\"model\":\"anthropic/claude-haiku-5.5\",\"messages\":[{\"role\":\"system\",\"content\":\"You check an illustration plan before it is drawn. You get the moment's text with its neighbours, the depiction rules, the section cast (id, name, hasForm), the plan's selected cast ids (`present`), its seven scene fields, any OWNER LOOK CONSTRAINTS that rendering will use, and the canon of the selected entries. Report only clear problems that a careful reader would agree with, and return an empty list when the plan is a reasonable illustration of the moment. Do not report preferences, small omissions or other valid readings. Return only JSON.\\nThe text decides who is in the scene; canon decides how they look; the scene plan decides this moment's place, time, light, clothing and action. Owner look constraints, when given, are binding.\\nKinds:\\n- unselected_figure: a section cast entry (a person, group, place, object, or a no-form presence shown as its effect) is clearly depicted in a scene field but its id is not in present. Use its id.\\n- outside_instant: a selected or described person or presence does not belong in this moment, such as a speaker, writer, prophet or listener put into a scene their words only describe or made a figure of their own words, the narrator of a story or vision, someone from a different event, or a no-form presence the moment does not show. Use its id, or empty.\\n- not_one_instant: the fields give someone incompatible poses or places, or show successive steps as one image.\\n- embodied_formless: a hasForm false entry is given a body, face, hands, clothing, a robe or train, a silhouette, a throne or seat of its own, or is described as seated or standing.\\n- look_conflict: an OWNER LOOK CONSTRAINTS value (only when supplied) contradicts the scene, the text or the depiction rules. Quote that value.\\n- canon_conflict: a scene field contradicts a selected entry's fixed canon. Quote the scene field.\\n- missing_canon: the scene depicts a named recurring character or group with no section cast entry. Leave entryId empty.\\nFor each problem, copy a short exact phrase from a scene field or a selected id into planQuote (from an owner constraint for look_conflict) and give a one-sentence reason.\"},{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":\"DEPICTION RULES\\n- God the Father has no human face or body; use light, cloud, fire or radiance. The Holy Spirit is dove, wind or flame, never human.\\n- Treat battles, death and crucifixion seriously; avoid lingering gore.\\n- No sexually explicit content; non-sexual nudity may follow the text.\\n- Show all peoples with dignity, without ethnic or religious caricature.\\n- Visionary creatures follow the text, strange and fearsome rather than comic.\\nSTORY SECTION: The LORD descends on Sinai\\n\\nMOMENT (Exodus 19:18): Mount Sinai, the whole of it, smoked, because Yahweh descended on it in fire; and its smoke ascended like the smoke of a furnace, and the whole mountain quaked greatly.\\nPREVIOUS: Moses led the people out of the camp to meet God; and they stood at the lower part of the mountain.\\nNEXT: When the sound of the trumpet grew louder and louder, Moses spoke, and God answered him by a voice.\\n\\nSECTION CAST (id: name, hasForm):\\n- moses: Moses (hasForm: true)\\n- god: God / Yahweh, the Father and God of Israel (hasForm: false)\\n- mount_sinai: Mount Sinai (hasForm: true)\\n\\nSELECTED CANON (complete assigned stages; fixed identity, not source evidence):\\n- moses (stage: elder, kind: character, hasForm: true): Moses: a tall, lean man of eighty with a long white beard, in a coarse brown wool cloak and a shepherd's staff.\\n- mount_sinai (stage: main, kind: location, hasForm: true): Mount Sinai: a steep granite mountain of red-brown rock above a gravel plain.\\n- god (stage: main, kind: character, hasForm: false): God the Father: no human face or body; presence shown only as radiance, cloud and fire.\\n\\nPLAN\\npresent: moses, mount_sinai, god\\nprimarySubject: Mount Sinai wrapped in billowing smoke and fire\\naction: the mountain quakes as smoke rises like a furnace\\nsetting: the gravel plain at the foot of Sinai\\nsecondaryElements: Moses at the front of the trembling crowd\\nmood: awe and dread\\ntimeOfDay: morning under dark smoke\\ncomposition: wide view from the plain up to the summit\"}],\"response_format\":{\"type\":\"json_schema\",\"json_schema\":{\"name\":\"plan_review\",\"strict\":true,\"schema\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"problems\":{\"type\":\"array\",\"items\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"kind\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"enum\":[\"unselected_figure\",\"outside_instant\",\"not_one_instant\",\"embodied_formless\",\"look_conflict\",\"canon_conflict\",\"missing_canon\"]},\"entryId\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The cast id the problem concerns; empty when it has none.\"},\"planQuote\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"A short exact phrase from a look field for look_conflict; otherwise from a scene field or a selected id.\"},\"reason\":{\"type\":\"string\"}},\"required\":[\"kind\",\"entryId\",\"planQuote\",\"reason\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},\"required\":[\"problems\"],\"additionalProperties\":false}}},\"provider\":{\"require_parameters\":true,\"order\":[\"anthropic\"],\"allow_fallbacks\":false},\"reasoning\":{\"effort\":\"low\"},\"max_tokens\":4000,\"usage\":{\"include\":true}}",
